==Battleground==
*10 [[Croconator]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
*10 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[M. Ost]] spawns as the boss after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage can be played in a few ways due to the boss spawn timing.

==='''Strategy 1 (Rush)'''===
{{Lineup
|Richest Cat
|Lollycat
|Brah Cats
|Awakened Mina
|Holy Valkyrie Cat
|Courier Cat|50
|Jelly Dumpling Cat|50
|Manic Eraser Cat|50
|Awakened Bahamut Cat|40+
|?
|notes = *The final slot can be filled with anything else that helps in destroying bases.
*[[Offshore Accounts (Combo)|Offshore Accounts]] is required, but the other [[Cat Combo|Combos]] can be replaced with better alternatives.
}}

The main objective of this strategy is to destroy the stage before the R.Ost and M. Ost can spawn.

Send out [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]] whenever possible for the whole fight. When Courier gets his first hit on the [[Croconator]]s, start sending out [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Erasers]] too. When the second Courier lands his first hit, spawn a [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] to do damage to the [[Shibalien Elite]] and [[Doge Dark]]. If you don't own Jelly Dumpling, spawn Slime Cat when the first Courier lands his third hit. When you have the money, send out [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and you should be able to win the stage.

=== '''Strategy 2 (4 Crown Friendly/Cheese)''' ===
{{Lineup|Noodle Cats|Val Val Cat|Richest Cat|Riceball Cat|50|Jelly Dumpling Cat|50|Goemon Cat|Courier Cat|50|Idi:N2|50|Awakened Bahamut Cat|50|?|notes=*The "?" slot can be filled with another rusher, such as [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]], or a [[Cat Combo|combo]] slave, such as [[Maneki Cat (Special Cat)|Neo Maneki Cat]].
*[[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]] has the HP up MAX [[Talents|talent]].}}
Immediately send out [[Thief Cat (Rare Cat)|Goemon Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]], followed a second later by Riceball Cat, and another [[Thief Cat (Rare Cat)|Goemon Cat]]. [[Thief Cat (Rare Cat)|Goemon Cat]] should garner enough money from the [[Croconator]]s to spawn in [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], and eventually [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]]. These two, as well as the small stack of [[Thief Cat (Rare Cat)|Goemon Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]] should quickly whittle down the HP of the base before the [[M. Ost]] or [[R.Ost]] even spawns.

==Trivia==
*Choco Highlands' Japanese name, Guri Kōgen (グリ高原), is a pun on ''guriko'' (グリコ), a variation of [[wikipedia:Rock paper scissors|janken]] in which players have to take three or six steps up a flight of stairs depending on whether they use rock, paper or scissors to win; the player who reaches the top of the stairs first is the winner of the game. ''Kōgen'' (高原) means "plateau". Interestingly, Guri Kōgen also sounds identical to ''gurikōgen'' (グリコーゲン), the Japanese pronunciation of ''[[wikipedia:Glycogen|glycogen]]''.

